:A
ABOUT FILE TRANSFERS

A file transfer involves two programs: one sending and one receiving.
Entering the command at the RCP/M end is only half the job. Your terminal
must be ready to receive or send using the matching protocol.

SyncTERM supports the traditional transfer protocols. The board uses
YMODEM for downloads and XMODEM/CRC or YMODEM for uploads. Do not use
terminal text capture for binary files.

Completed uploads go to the sysop's private review inbox, rather than
WORK or the public collections. A useful submission should include
instructions, author and hardware information, and distribution terms.
